 "input": "how I do my self assessment as a freelancer. register for self assessment once, get the UTR. through the year keep invoices and receipts in the spreadsheet, the spreadsheet works out income and expenses. after April, download the P60 from my part-time job and interest figures from the bank. log into the HMRC online account, fill the return using the spreadsheet totals and the P60. HMRC calculates the bill. pay by 31 January (balancing payment plus first payment on account), payments on account are based on last year's bill. keep records 5 years in case of an enquiry.",
